with all the fanfare that befits egypt's  ancient kings and queens the highly  anticipated  and meticulously planned pharaoh's  golden parade  was the biggest cultural event cairo has  seen in recent years  traveling in individual vehicles  bedecked in ancient egyptian style  the mummified royals 22 of them in all  were moved from cairo's egyptian museum  in tahrir square they moved through the  capital streets to a new location  a state at the art facility called the  national museum of ancient civilization  [Music]  where they were greeted by a concert  from the cairo philharmonic  featuring famous singers and then  received by the egyptian president  the pharaohs are the staff of legend and  include amenhotep the first  ramses ii ramsay's the third and queen  nefertari  you've got two worlds really coming  together you've got the curators who  normally move these things  without the world watching and prepare  objects to travel around the world but  then you've got a spectacle that needs  to be put on  so the logistics behind it were very  complex and you can imagine they've been  working for a very long time and i think  they've really pulled it off it's got  their spectacle  but we also felt that everything was  done safely  the security operation was a mammoth  undertaking streets were closed and  cairo  brought to a standstill the event which  lasted around two hours  was attended by various dignitaries  including the director general of unesco  the un's world heritage organization  once the mummies arrived at their new  resting place they are to be put into  restoration in a lab for 15 days  and readied for display but there are a  minority who muttered darkly  about an ancient curse legend has it  that cursed will be the ones that move  the mummies  they say the suez canal blockage  disturbing global markets  two trains colliding with each other a  garment factory blaze and a residential  building collapse  all came after the announcement of the  pharaoh's golden parade  but the ancient curse hasn't stopped the  pharaohs once again  appearing on the streets of egypt  imran khan al jazeera
 

